# The eval scene set: goal, spawn bound, and why. ONE place, so no hand-written
# command can drop a parameter again.
#
# SPAWN_MAX matters: with a FIXED goal frame, a spawn drawn AFTER that frame puts
# the goal behind a forward-only robot, which then needs a ~164 deg spin before it
# can move at all. Every arm failed quad2_00 episode 1 for exactly this reason
# (2026-09-23, Joana spotted it in the trajectories).
#
# SPAWN_MAX alone is not enough for a CORNER test: spawning 8 frames before the
# goal puts the robot past the bend, so there is nothing to turn around. The old
# correct runs were named spawn12-22_goal48 -- 26-36 frames of approach, so the
# robot must reach the bend, turn, and continue (2026-09-23, Joana).
#
# MEASURED with scripts/scene_bend.py, not copied off an old folder name:
#   quad2_00     bend at frames 25-45;  spawn 12-22 -> 254 deg of turning to the goal, 13 deg inside
#   sequoia1_17  bend starts at frame 50; 40-56 put 58 deg INSIDE the spawn range, so 34-48 instead
#
# TESTDIST (2026-09-24) is the distance the robot must actually DRIVE, in metres --
# the path AROUND the bend, not the straight line to the goal. On a corner those are
# very different: quad2_00_far is 8.1 m straight but 13.6 m along the walkway, and
# sizing its budget on 8.1 m gave 170 actions for a course needing ~258. Use the
# geodesic figure scene_corner_scan.py prints (straight x detour); for an open scene
# the two are the same number. Without it the
# episode budget is sized from each ARM's curriculum reach, so on the identical
# 8.1 m far corner chunk5 (reach 4 m) got 104 actions and memDINO_warm (reach
# 7.5 m) got 160 -- and 104 actions cannot cover 8.1 m at any throttle chunk5 has
# shown. Its TIMEOUT was the budget, not the policy (Joana: "this one seems to
# time out too early"). A short test never shrinks a longer curriculum's budget.
#
# format:  <scene> <goal spec> <spawn bounds, comma separated, or ->   # note
EVAL_SCENES="
quad1_01     GOALFRAMERANGE=15,70   -        TESTDIST=8.4   # open plaza; graded, 3.9-8.4 m measured
quad1_07     GOALFRAMERANGE=15,70   -        TESTDIST=8.4   # second plaza (duplicate of quad1_01, usually skip)
quad2_00     GOAL_FRAME=48          SPAWN_MIN=13,SPAWN_MAX=18   TESTDIST=8.8   # GRASS corner. Spawns 12 and 19-22 dropped: they fail the 0.4 m jitter clearance. 8.8 m is the walk from spawn 13, measured 2026-09-24
sequoia1_10  GOAL_FRAME=30          SPAWN_MIN=5,SPAWN_MAX=18    TESTDIST=3.9   # pedestrians, NOT in training
sequoia1_17  GOAL_FRAME=69          SPAWN_MIN=43,SPAWN_MAX=48   TESTDIST=9.8   # DIRT/ROUGH corner: classify_pair calls all 6 spawns corner+narrow, detour 1.16-1.18, corridor 0.89 m. Measured 2026-09-24; the old 72/34-48 was never checked
quad2_04_ped GOAL_FRAME=66          SPAWN_MIN=29,SPAWN_MAX=36   TESTDIST=9.4 SCENE=quad2_04  # PEDESTRIAN: a 5064-point person stands ~5 m along and 0.21-0.27 m off the straight line, at every spawn in the window; the robot is 0.30 m wide and the person ~0.45 m, so they block the centreline. Goal 66 rather than 60 so there are ~4 m of approach AND ~4 m past the person (Joana, 2026-09-24). Spawn 28 fails the jitter clearance.
sequoia1_21  GOAL_FRAME=45          SPAWN_MIN=7,SPAWN_MAX=14    TESTDIST=11.4  # DIRT/ROUGH corner (24.6% rough): the walk bends at frames 25-35; spawn before it, goal after. 52% of the straight line is blocked at spawn 7 even though the detour ratio reads 1.12 -- the ratio undersells a short way round on a 10 m line. All 8 spawns clear the jitter. Joana chose this terrain over sequoia1_17 (2026-09-24). Straight-line to the goal is 9.0-9.8 m, beyond most arms' curriculum: flag as out-of-distribution for arms under 9 m.
quad2_00_far GOAL_FRAME=55          SPAWN_MIN=5,SPAWN_MAX=12    SCENE=quad2_00 TESTDIST=13.6  # the WALK length spawn->goal, which is what the robot drives around the bend. Do NOT size this from the label grid: quad2_00's grid is mostly void (see day_0924/corner_check/) and its detour reads 1.02, which is an artefact of a sparse map, not the course. spawn 2.2-3.0 m
                                                                                # along, bend at 6.8-10.8 m,
                                                                                # goal at 13.6 m -- the turn is
                                                                                # unmistakable on a path plot
"

# gnd -- the only HONESTLY held-out environment. Every campus clip sits within 30 m
# of a training clip, so no campus scene is truly out of distribution; gnd is a
# different site entirely. Frames there are 0.38 m apart against campus's 0.23-0.37,
# so a goal frame chosen by campus habit lands far outside the trained band -- these
# were measured with scripts/scene_bend.py to sit at 5.3-7.9 m (2026-09-24).
# Clips live in data/gnd_clips, not campus_clips, hence the CLIPS= column.
EVAL_SCENES_GND="
gnd_AU_180   GOAL_FRAME=32   SPAWN_MIN=10,SPAWN_MAX=16  CLIPS=gnd_clips TESTDIST=6.9  # 21 deg and the straight line is walkable: OPEN navigation, not a corner
gnd_AUw360   GOAL_FRAME=40   SPAWN_MIN=13,SPAWN_MAX=18  CLIPS=gnd_clips TESTDIST=6.1  # straight line is walkable so path = straight. The WALK turns 151 deg but nothing blocks the straight line: an open turn, so it does not test obstacle avoidance (Joana, 2026-09-24)
# BROKEN, do not run until re-measured. NOT a grass spawn: every frame 20-25 is
# walkable. They carry only 0.41 m of clearance, and eval jitters the spawn 0.4 m
# laterally (SPAWNJLAT), which walks the robot onto the boundary -- hence a crash at
# step 1, not step 0, in 16/16 episodes of both arms. A spawn frame must clear
# body/2 + the jitter, which scene_corner_scan.py --jitter now enforces. The same
# scene DOES hold a real corner at goal 46 (detour 1.16); pick its window with:
#   python scripts/scene_corner_scan.py gnd_AUw170 --band 5 8
# gnd_AUw170   GOAL_FRAME=45   SPAWN_MIN=20,SPAWN_MAX=25  CLIPS=gnd_clips TESTDIST=7.0
"
EVAL_SCENES="${EVAL_SCENES}${EVAL_SCENES_GND}"

# The three-scene core set: open navigation, turning, and a scene held out of training.
EVAL_CORE="quad1_01 quad2_00 sequoia1_10"
# The three scenarios Jing asked for (2026-09-24), each defined by measurement rather
# than by a scene name: grass corner, dirt/rough corner, and a person in the way.
EVAL_SCENARIOS="quad2_00 sequoia1_21 quad2_04_ped"
# The held-out set: one open, two corners, a different site.
# AUw170 is out until its spawn window is re-measured; AUw360 is an OPEN turn, so
# neither held-out scene currently tests turning around an obstacle. Finding one is
# what scene_corner_scan.py is for.
EVAL_GND="gnd_AU_180 gnd_AUw360"
